  @Description_9fa970e65e3c = N'Sakana AI''s cost-performance orchestration model, released September 11, 2026. Fugu is not a single model but a learned multi-agent orchestrator: a language model trained to route each task across a fixed pool of open-weight and specialist models (including NVIDIA''s Nemotron family) and to recursively call instances of itself, then stitch the results together. Fugu Max dynamically selects efficient combinations of expert agents to improve quality and cost together. 1,048,576-token context window, 128,000-token maximum output, priced flat regardless of context length. Accepts text, image and PDF input and returns text. Supports function calling, structured (JSON) outputs via response_format, configurable reasoning effort (high, xhigh, max), and built-in web search and web fetch (billed separately at $10 per 1,000 search calls, which MJ does not model). Reached here through OpenRouter (sakana/fugu-max); Sakana''s own OpenAI-compatible API is not wired up because MJ has no Sakana driver class yet. Note: Sakana does not serve the Fugu family inside the EU or EEA pending GDPR compliance work.'
